    {
      "id": "ee1Wme0e56BuiZGTzxcoE",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 962.0406772779979,
      "y": 1918.7753261863281,
      "width": 1188,
      "height": 375,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2sV",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 646135776,
      "version": 891,
      "versionNonce": 449549169,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793529517488,
      "created": 1792936281672,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Follow-up questions\n- Realtime host dies, 1M conns reconnect at once?\n    -> client reconnects with exponential backoff + jitter, L4 spreads to other hosts, on connect pull Inbox\n- Host crashes after Message written, before Inbox fanout?\n    -> sender gets no ack -> retry with same clientMsgId -> server dedup\n- Redis pub/sub single node can't handle ~1M publish/s? Redis down?\n    -> Redis Cluster sharded pub/sub, shard by userId; Redis down -> msgs still in Inbox, delivered by sweep / reconnect\n- Why not Kafka?\n    -> topic per user impossible, consumer rebalance slow, built for throughput not ms-level point-to-point push\n- Group fanout to 100 inboxes on send path, latency ok?\n    -> BatchWriteItem 25/batch, 4 batches in parallel, tens of ms; ack sender after fanout\n- Ordering across senders on different hosts?\n    -> seq = server timestamp, tolerate ms-level clock skew (no per-chat counter: contention)\n- Multi-device?\n    -> Client table, Inbox & channel per clientId, each device acks separately",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Follow-up questions\n- Realtime host dies, 1M conns reconnect at once?\n    -> client reconnects with exponential backoff + jitter, L4 spreads to other hosts, on connect pull Inbox\n- Host crashes after Message written, before Inbox fanout?\n    -> sender gets no ack -> retry with same clientMsgId -> server dedup\n- Redis pub/sub single node can't handle ~1M publish/s? Redis down?\n    -> Redis Cluster sharded pub/sub, shard by userId; Redis down -> msgs still in Inbox, delivered by sweep / reconnect\n- Why not Kafka?\n    -> topic per user impossible, consumer rebalance slow, built for throughput not ms-level point-to-point push\n- Group fanout to 100 inboxes on send path, latency ok?\n    -> BatchWriteItem 25/batch, 4 batches in parallel, tens of ms; ack sender after fanout\n- Ordering across senders on different hosts?\n    -> seq = server timestamp, tolerate ms-level clock skew (no per-chat counter: contention)\n- Multi-device?\n    -> Client table, Inbox & channel per clientId, each device acks separately",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "OmMG9Lhf-74N8Nkmk26Q5",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 962,
      "y": 1600,
      "width": 1524.6000000000001,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2sVV",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1404277497,
      "version": 809,
      "versionNonce": 2013157407,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1793529517488,
      "created": 1792936673892,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Deep dive 2: how to store msg/inbox temporary?\n- DynamoDB TTL (expireAt = ts + 30d, deleted in background, no WCU), S3 lifecycle rule for attachments\n\nDeep dive 3: group fanout writes 100 Inbox rows per msg, ok at 1B scale?\n- cost: ~1M msg/s * avg fanout ~5 -> ~5M Inbox writes/s (~5M WCU, tens of $K/day provisioned, on-demand far more)\n- fanout on write (current): read on connect is 1 query by clientId, write amplification = group size, so cap group at 100\n- fanout on read: 1 Message row per msg, each client keeps cursor (chatId -> last seq), on connect query each chat after cursor\n    - write cost flat, read cost = number of chats, fits large groups / channels (> 1000 members)\n- hybrid (pick this): fanout on write for groups <= 100 (DM + small group = most traffic), fanout on read for large channels\n- cut writes further: skip Inbox for online recipients, write Inbox only if no recv ack in T s (saves most writes, but host crash within T loses tracking)",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Deep dive 2: how to store msg/inbox temporary?\n- DynamoDB TTL (expireAt = ts + 30d, deleted in background, no WCU), S3 lifecycle rule for attachments\n\nDeep dive 3: group fanout writes 100 Inbox rows per msg, ok at 1B scale?\n- cost: ~1M msg/s * avg fanout ~5 -> ~5M Inbox writes/s (~5M WCU, tens of $K/day provisioned, on-demand far more)\n- fanout on write (current): read on connect is 1 query by clientId, write amplification = group size, so cap group at 100\n- fanout on read: 1 Message row per msg, each client keeps cursor (chatId -> last seq), on connect query each chat after cursor\n    - write cost flat, read cost = number of chats, fits large groups / channels (> 1000 members)\n- hybrid (pick this): fanout on write for groups <= 100 (DM + small group = most traffic), fanout on read for large channels\n- cut writes further: skip Inbox for online recipients, write Inbox only if no recv ack in T s (saves most writes, but host crash within T loses tracking)",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
    {
      "id": "MvbF27o6UfOcL44dRS8ll",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 330.97308349609375,
      "y": 134.2828826904297,
      "width": 715,
      "height": 525,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2t",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1742470207,
      "version": 940,
      "versionNonce": 887905471,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1793587565715,
      "created": 1793529520284,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "TopK Youtube views\n\nFunctional requirements\n- Count the views of each video\n- Query the topK views of all the video by a given time window\n    - support \"hour / day / month / all time\" from now (tumbling)\n    - do not support any given time window do not start from now\n\nNon-functional requirements\n- CAP: availability >> consistency (eventually consistent, < 1m)\n- latency: query < tens of ms (precompute + cache)\n- precise: exact counts (approximation as deep dive)\n- scale: large volume of videos, high throughput\n\nCore entities\n- Video\n- View\n\nAPI\n- query topK views\nGET /views/topK?timeWindow={}&k={} -> [videoId, viewCount]",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "TopK Youtube views\n\nFunctional requirements\n- Count the views of each video\n- Query the topK views of all the video by a given time window\n    - support \"hour / day / month / all time\" from now (tumbling)\n    - do not support any given time window do not start from now\n\nNon-functional requirements\n- CAP: availability >> consistency (eventually consistent, < 1m)\n- latency: query < tens of ms (precompute + cache)\n- precise: exact counts (approximation as deep dive)\n- scale: large volume of videos, high throughput\n\nCore entities\n- Video\n- View\n\nAPI\n- query topK views\nGET /views/topK?timeWindow={}&k={} -> [videoId, viewCount]",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
