    {
      "id": "n0S13nILqKJ3JukWWkPWP",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1239.510046155541,
      "y": 581.7360467489412,
      "width": 1001,
      "height": 1525,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b3M",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 506940369,
      "version": 18,
      "versionNonce": 1602849663,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1793601464825,
      "created": 1793530675630,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Deep dive\n\n1. How to handle hot videos (hot write)?\n- partition by videoId, salt hot videos only: videoId:0-N\n- Flink aggregates by salted key, strips the suffix on output\n- DB merges partial counts: views = views + count (order doesn't matter)\n- hot list: static (big creators) | dynamic (threshold -> config)\n- not random partition + 2-stage agg -> every video pays an extra shuffle\n\n2. How to shard the aggregator?\n- shard = hash(videoId) % P (strip salt first), aligned with DB shards\n- size depends on active videos per minute, not raw view QPS\n- each shard keeps its own top K -> merge P x K into the global top K\n  - option1: Merger (cron, every 1min) -> Redis -> stable latency (good)\n  - option2: Query Service merges online + cache -> stampede on expiry\n- versioned key top-k:{window}:{minute}:shard:{i} to align shards\n\n3. How to support sliding windows?\n- step: hour -> minute, day -> hour, month -> day\n- counts: +new (consumer group) | -old (consumer group lagging one window)\n  - both read the Flink agg topic -> subtract exactly what was added\n- top K with decrements: heap can't see the replacement video\n  - hour: ZSET per shard (active videos only) -> exact\n  - day / month: K' > K candidates + periodic rebuild -> approximate | keep tumbling\n\n4. How to handle hot reads?\n- local cache in Query Service (refresh 5-10s) + Redis replicas + CDN\n- versioned key + pointer switch; serve stale when Merger lags\n\n5. How to reduce cost with approximation? (only if precision is relaxed)\n- Count-Min Sketch (d x w counters, overestimate only, error <= eps * N) + top K candidates\n- hour: eps = 1e-6, d = 5 -> ~54MB, error <= ~2900 views\n- all in memory (Flink state), no DB\n- sliding: subtract only what was added (lagging consumer), no conservative update\n- need exact counts -> offline Kafka -> S3 -> Spark (lambda)\n\n6. Fault tolerance\n- Kafka: replication 3, retention >= max(window, checkpoint interval)\n- Flink: checkpoint (state + offset) + replay\n- Aggregator (DB): applied(shard, minute) in the same transaction -> idempotent +=\n- Aggregator (CMS): snapshot (CMS + candidates + offset) to S3 -> restore, seek, replay\n- Merger / Query Service: stateless, Redis overwrite (idempotent), serve stale\n\n7. Do we still need the DB? (Flink state + heap + checkpoint)\n- Kafka -> Flink 1min agg -> keyBy(videoId): counts in keyed state\n  -> keyBy(window, shard): heap per window -> Merger -> Redis\n- checkpoint: counts + heaps + Kafka offset -> S3\n- exact counts ~ hundreds of GB -> RocksDB state backend (DB embedded in Flink)\n  - CMS: ~tens of MB -> truly in memory\n- incremental checkpoint; recovery = download state + replay (minutes, serve stale)\n- fallback: archive raw events to S3 (data lake) -> Spark recompute -> State Processor API\n  (corrupted state / incompatible upgrade can't be fixed by checkpoint)\n\n                 DB counts + heap          | Flink state + heap + checkpoint\n  write cost:    4 tables upsert / 1min    | local RocksDB update\n  components:    Flink + Aggregator + DB    | Flink (+ S3)\n  recovery:      counts safe, rebuild heap | download checkpoint + replay\n  fallback:      DB itself                 | S3 data lake + batch recompute\n  per-video/audit: query DB                | offline / async to OLAP\n  interview risk: low                      | need RocksDB, checkpoint, state migration\n- know Flink well -> right side as main line; otherwise -> left side",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "baseFontSize": null,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Deep dive\n\n1. How to handle hot videos (hot write)?\n- partition by videoId, salt hot videos only: videoId:0-N\n- Flink aggregates by salted key, strips the suffix on output\n- DB merges partial counts: views = views + count (order doesn't matter)\n- hot list: static (big creators) | dynamic (threshold -> config)\n- not random partition + 2-stage agg -> every video pays an extra shuffle\n\n2. How to shard the aggregator?\n- shard = hash(videoId) % P (strip salt first), aligned with DB shards\n- size depends on active videos per minute, not raw view QPS\n- each shard keeps its own top K -> merge P x K into the global top K\n  - option1: Merger (cron, every 1min) -> Redis -> stable latency (good)\n  - option2: Query Service merges online + cache -> stampede on expiry\n- versioned key top-k:{window}:{minute}:shard:{i} to align shards\n\n3. How to support sliding windows?\n- step: hour -> minute, day -> hour, month -> day\n- counts: +new (consumer group) | -old (consumer group lagging one window)\n  - both read the Flink agg topic -> subtract exactly what was added\n- top K with decrements: heap can't see the replacement video\n  - hour: ZSET per shard (active videos only) -> exact\n  - day / month: K' > K candidates + periodic rebuild -> approximate | keep tumbling\n\n4. How to handle hot reads?\n- local cache in Query Service (refresh 5-10s) + Redis replicas + CDN\n- versioned key + pointer switch; serve stale when Merger lags\n\n5. How to reduce cost with approximation? (only if precision is relaxed)\n- Count-Min Sketch (d x w counters, overestimate only, error <= eps * N) + top K candidates\n- hour: eps = 1e-6, d = 5 -> ~54MB, error <= ~2900 views\n- all in memory (Flink state), no DB\n- sliding: subtract only what was added (lagging consumer), no conservative update\n- need exact counts -> offline Kafka -> S3 -> Spark (lambda)\n\n6. Fault tolerance\n- Kafka: replication 3, retention >= max(window, checkpoint interval)\n- Flink: checkpoint (state + offset) + replay\n- Aggregator (DB): applied(shard, minute) in the same transaction -> idempotent +=\n- Aggregator (CMS): snapshot (CMS + candidates + offset) to S3 -> restore, seek, replay\n- Merger / Query Service: stateless, Redis overwrite (idempotent), serve stale\n\n7. Do we still need the DB? (Flink state + heap + checkpoint)\n- Kafka -> Flink 1min agg -> keyBy(videoId): counts in keyed state\n  -> keyBy(window, shard): heap per window -> Merger -> Redis\n- checkpoint: counts + heaps + Kafka offset -> S3\n- exact counts ~ hundreds of GB -> RocksDB state backend (DB embedded in Flink)\n  - CMS: ~tens of MB -> truly in memory\n- incremental checkpoint; recovery = download state + replay (minutes, serve stale)\n- fallback: archive raw events to S3 (data lake) -> Spark recompute -> State Processor API\n  (corrupted state / incompatible upgrade can't be fixed by checkpoint)\n\n                 DB counts + heap          | Flink state + heap + checkpoint\n  write cost:    4 tables upsert / 1min    | local RocksDB update\n  components:    Flink + Aggregator + DB    | Flink (+ S3)\n  recovery:      counts safe, rebuild heap | download checkpoint + replay\n  fallback:      DB itself                 | S3 data lake + batch recompute\n  per-video/audit: query DB                | offline / async to OLAP\n  interview risk: low                      | need RocksDB, checkpoint, state migration\n- know Flink well -> right side as main line; otherwise -> left side",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "labelPosition": null
    },
